.Dd April 14, 2026
.Dt PODCAST-MGR.ISO12207 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm podcast-mgr.iso12207
.Nd software lifecycle process record per ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2017
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This document records the software lifecycle processes applied to
.Nm podcast-mgr
version 1.0 in accordance with ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2017
.Em Systems and software engineering \(em Software life cycle processes .
.Pp
.Nm podcast-mgr
is a two-component system:
.Bl -tag -width "podcast.sh"
.It Nm index.cgi
A FastCGI single-page application that manages a podcast subscription
database stored as
.Pa feeds.xml .
.It Nm podcast.sh
A tcsh cron script that reads
.Pa feeds.xml
and downloads podcast episodes according to the schedule defined therein.
.El
.Pp
The components are intentionally decoupled.
.Nm index.cgi
writes; the cron job reads.
.Sh STAKEHOLDER NEEDS AND REQUIREMENTS (6.4.1)
.Ss Context
Single operator.
Local-network deployment on a POSIX host running a FastCGI-capable
HTTP server.
No internet-exposed surface.
No multi-user access.
.Ss Needs
.Bl -enum
.It
The operator shall be able to add, edit, and remove podcast feed
subscriptions through a web browser without editing XML by hand.
.It
The subscription database shall be consumed by a scheduled cron job
without operator intervention.
.It
The system shall not perform any network I/O itself; downloads are
delegated to
.Nm podcast.sh .
.It
The system shall preserve
.Pa feeds.xml
integrity across write failures.
.It
The system shall not require installation of a runtime interpreter or
virtual machine.
.El
.Sh SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS (6.4.2)
.Bl -tag -width "SYS-05"
.It Sy SYS-01
The system shall parse
.Pa feeds.xml
at worker startup and hold the subscription list in memory for the
worker lifetime.
.It Sy SYS-02
The system shall validate all form submissions against the field
constraints defined in
.Pa feeds.xsd
before writing.
.It Sy SYS-03
Writes to
.Pa feeds.xml
shall be atomic: a temporary file shall be written and renamed over
the target; the original shall be untouched on any failure.
.It Sy SYS-04
The system shall reject
.Pa feeds.xml
if it is a symbolic link, not a regular file, or exceeds 512\ KB.
.It Sy SYS-05
The worker process shall reduce its privilege after startup using the
platform-appropriate sandboxing mechanism
.Pq seccomp, Capsicum, or pledge .
.It Sy SYS-06
The build shall require only a C compiler and the kcgi library;
no interpreted language runtime shall be required at build or run time.
.El
.Sh SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS (6.4.3)
.Bl -tag -width "SWR-10"
.It Sy SWR-01
.Nm index.cgi
shall implement the routes defined in
.Xr index.cgi 8 ,
section
.Sx ROUTES .
.It Sy SWR-02
All htmx partial responses shall be generated via
.Fn kxml ;
the SPA root document shall be generated via
.Fn khtml .
.It Sy SWR-03
The field definition table
.Vt FieldDef FIELDS[]
shall be the single source of truth for XML attribute names, form
labels, input types, length caps, and enumerated option lists.
.It Sy SWR-04
String views pointing into kcgi request memory shall be arena-copied
before
.Fn khttp_free
is called.
.It Sy SWR-05
.Nm xml_node_serialize
shall not be called; output shall be constructed via
.Vt XMLString
directly to avoid the self-closing node serialisation defect in
mrvladus/xml.h.
.It Sy SWR-06
.Nm podcast.sh
shall validate
.Pa feeds.xml
against
.Pa feeds.xsd
using
.Xr xmlstarlet 1
before processing any feeds.
.It Sy SWR-07
.Nm podcast.sh
shall initialise
.Va temp_files
as an empty list
.Pq Li "set temp_files = ()"
to prevent phantom elements in the cleanup loop.
.It Sy SWR-08
The exit paths in
.Fn main
shall use a single
.Ic goto
label with a NULL-guarded
.Fn khttp_fcgi_free
call.
.El
.Sh SOFTWARE ARCHITECTURE (6.4.5)
.Ss Process Model
.Nm index.cgi
operates as a persistent FastCGI worker.
One worker process services all requests sequentially.
The process lifecycle is:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Load and validate
.Pa feeds.xml
into the root arena.
.It
Call
.Fn sandbox_lockdown_rw
to reduce privilege.
.It
Enter the
.Fn khttp_fcgi_parse
accept loop.
.It
Dispatch each request by page enum; render response; call
.Fn khttp_free .
.It
On loop exit, free fcgi handle and destroy arena.
.El
.Ss Memory Model
All worker-lifetime allocations use a single 4\ MB root arena.
Per-request string copies from kcgi fieldmap are also placed in this
arena.
The arena is never reset between requests; it grows monotonically and
is destroyed on process exit.
xml.h heap allocations (from
.Fn xml_parse_string )
are freed via
.Fn xml_node_free
after attribute strings are copied into the arena.
.Ss Data Flow
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Browser sends GET or POST to nginx/lighttpd FastCGI proxy.
.It
kcgi parses request; populates
.Vt struct kreq .
.It
Route dispatch selects handler.
.It
Mutating handlers update in-memory
.Vt PodcastArray ,
call
.Fn write_feeds_xml ,
then render the updated list partial.
.It
On write failure, in-memory state is restored from a pre-mutation
snapshot.
.El
.Ss Component Dependencies
.Bl -tag -width "mrvladus/xml.h"
.It kcgi
FastCGI framing, field parsing, HTML/XML output.
.It mrvladus/xml.h
XML parse on startup only.
.It tsoding/sv
String view type used for all in-memory attribute storage.
.It arena.h
Region allocator; caller-supplied.
.It sandbox.h
Platform-dispatch privilege-drop; caller-supplied.
.El
